## Why This Is Asked
This question tests data governance and cloud IAM proficiency in regulated fintech environments, focusing on data lake isolation and rapid IR.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC with tenant attributes
- Deny-by-default bucket policies
- Data-centric protection (field-level encryption/tokenization)
- Policy drift detection (IAM Access Analyzer, CloudTrail)
- Incident response for data leakage (IR playbook, forensics)

## Code Example
```javascript
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Action": "*",
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringNotEquals": {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/tenant_id": "{tenant_id}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the policy in dev/stage? 
- What metrics indicate policy drift has been mitigated?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to apply multi-tenant isolation, data governance, and IR planning in a Databricks context beyond generic concepts.

## Key Concepts

- Unity Catalog RBAC and object-level permissions
- Tenant-scoped secret scopes and secret management
- Dynamic data masking and access controls for notebooks
- Audit logs and SIEM integration for detection
- Incident response playbooks and metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
